<article class="paper-card">
  <h2>Unpacking AI Bias and the Antidiscrimination Law Dilemma</h2>
  <p class="authors">Hoang Pham, Hannah Cha, and Rashon Poole</p>
  <p><strong>Stanford Law Review Online</strong> · <time datetime="2026-09-01">September 1, 2026</time></p>
  <p>What should AI systems represent: existing social patterns or a more inclusive future? We argue that many disputes over AI bias reflect disagreements about these goals, rather than technical flaws alone. The essay examines how these disagreements complicate the application of antidiscrimination law to AI.</p>
  <p>We propose an approach grounded in questions about each system’s purpose, deployment context, and competing values to help stakeholders assess bias and identify appropriate responses.</p>
